{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113089","id":3038022781,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc61FIx9","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113089","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113089.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113089.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113089","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113089/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113089/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113089/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/1013c914b904cacdab592c36526708dc21fed476","number":113089,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Optimize `AHashMap` lookups","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I did some adjustments in `AHashMap` which seemed to have increased performance in some situations.\r\n\r\n### Removed the `_elements` check from `_lookup_idx_with_hash()`\r\nThere is already a validity check of `_elements` in `_lookup_idx()`, so by having it in `lookup_idx_with_hash()` too means double check.\r\n\r\nThis affects every function of `AHashMap` that uses `_lookup_idx()`: `get()`, `getptr()`, `has()`, `erase()`, `replace_key()`, `find()`, `const &operator[]` and `get_index()`.\r\n\r\nChecks were added where `_lookup_idx_with_hash()` are called outside `_lookup_idx()`.\r\n\r\nConsequently, this makes most `AHashMap` lookup calls in pair with `HashMap`. `_lookup_idx_with_hash()` pretty much becomes `AHashMap`'s version of `HashMap::_lookup_idx_unchecked()`.\r\n\r\n### Removed the `unlikely` conditions from `AHashMap` lookups.\r\nSimply because the benchmarks below over the change above on my end showed it was slightly faster.\r\n\r\n### More versions of `_lookup_idx()` to remove the need of declaring a meta index\r\nSome meta index declarations exist for the sole purpose of providing a value for `_lookup_idx()` to handle.\r\n\r\nOn my end, duplicating code to avoid handling a meta index resulted in faster execution.\r\n\r\n## Benchmarks\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary><strong>PC specs</strong></summary>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><strong>CPU</strong>: Intel Core i5-11400H 2.70GHz</li>\r\n<li><strong>GPU</strong>: NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1650</li>\r\n<li><strong>RAM</strong>: 16GB (2x8 DDR4-3200) </li>\r\n<li><strong>OS</strong>: Linux (CachyOS) </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary><strong>Benchmark file</strong></summary>\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\n#include <chrono>\r\n#include <cstdio>\r\n\r\n#include \"core/templates/a_hash_map.h\"\r\n\r\n#undef WARN_VERBOSE\r\n#define WARN_VERBOSE ()\r\n\r\ntemplate <bool p_ensure_zero>\r\nvoid *Memory::alloc_static(size_t p_bytes, bool p_pad_align) {\r\n\tvoid *mem;\r\n\tif constexpr (p_ensure_zero) {\r\n\t\tmem = calloc(1, p_bytes);\r\n\t} else {\r\n\t\tmem = malloc(p_bytes);\r\n\t}\r\n\treturn mem;\r\n}\r\n\r\nvoid *Memory::realloc_static(void *p_memory, size_t p_bytes, bool p_pad_align) {\r\n\tif (p_memory == nullptr) {\r\n\t\treturn alloc_static<false>(p_bytes, p_pad_align);\r\n\t}\r\n\r\n\treturn realloc(p_memory, p_bytes);\r\n}\r\n\r\nvoid Memory::free_static(void *p_memory, bool p_pad_align) {\r\n\tif (p_memory) {\r\n\t\tfree(p_memory);\r\n\t}\r\n}\r\n\r\n\r\nstatic void get(AHashMap<uint32_t, int32_t> &map) {\r\n\tprintf(\"Benchmarking non-const get\\n\");\r\n\tauto start = std::chrono::system_clock::now();\r\n\tfor (int i = 0; i < 50000000; i++) {\r\n\t\tint32_t v = map.get(i);\r\n\t}\r\n\tauto end = std::chrono::system_clock::now();\r\n\tstd::chrono::duration<double> elapsed_seconds = end - start;\r\n\tprintf(\"%f\\n\", elapsed_seconds);\r\n}\r\n\r\nvoid getptr(AHashMap<uint32_t, int32_t> &map) {\r\n\tprintf(\"Benchmarking getptr\\n\");\r\n\tauto start = std::chrono::system_clock::now();\r\n\tfor (int i = 0; i < 50000000; i++) {\r\n\t\tint32_t *v = map.getptr(i);\r\n\t}\r\n\tauto end = std::chrono::system_clock::now();\r\n\tstd::chrono::duration<double> elapsed_seconds = end - start;\r\n\tprintf(\"%f\\n\", elapsed_seconds);\r\n}\r\n\r\nvoid has(AHashMap<uint32_t, int32_t> &map) {\r\n\tprintf(\"Benchmarking has\\n\");\r\n\tauto start = std::chrono::system_clock::now();\r\n\tfor (int i = 0; i < 50000000; i++) {\r\n\t\tbool has = map.has(i);\r\n\t}\r\n\tauto end = std::chrono::system_clock::now();\r\n\tstd::chrono::duration<double> elapsed_seconds = end - start;\r\n\tprintf(\"%f\\n\", elapsed_seconds);\r\n}\r\n\r\nvoid constiterator_find(AHashMap<uint32_t, int32_t> &map) {\r\n\tprintf(\"Benchmarking constiterator_find\\n\");\r\n\tauto start = std::chrono::system_clock::now();\r\n\tfor (int i = 0; i < 50000000; i++) {\r\n\t\tAHashMap<uint32_t, int32_t>::ConstIterator it = map.find(i);\r\n\t}\r\n\tauto end = std::chrono::system_clock::now();\r\n\tstd::chrono::duration<double> elapsed_seconds = end - start;\r\n\tprintf(\"%f\\n\", elapsed_seconds);\r\n}\r\n\r\nvoid iterator_find(AHashMap<uint32_t, int32_t> &map) {\r\n\tprintf(\"Benchmarking iterator_find\\n\");\r\n\tauto start = std::chrono::system_clock::now();\r\n\tfor (int i = 0; i < 50000000; i++) {\r\n\t\tAHashMap<uint32_t, int32_t>::Iterator it = map.find(i);\r\n\t}\r\n\tauto end = std::chrono::system_clock::now();\r\n\tstd::chrono::duration<double> elapsed_seconds = end - start;\r\n\tprintf(\"%f\\n\", elapsed_seconds);\r\n}\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nint main() {\r\n\tAHashMap<uint32_t, int32_t> map;\r\n\tmap.reserve(50000000);\r\n\tfor (int i = 0; i < 50000000; i++) {\r\n\t\tmap.insert_new(i, i * 2);\r\n\t}\r\n\r\n\t// Filled runs\r\n\tprintf(\"Benchmark case: filled maps\\n\");\r\n\tget(map);\r\n\tgetptr(map);\r\n\thas(map);\r\n\tconstiterator_find(map);\r\n\titerator_find(map);\r\n\r\n\t// Empty runs\r\n\tmap.reset();\r\n\tprintf(\"Benchmark case: empty maps\\n\");\r\n\tgetptr(map);\r\n\thas(map);\r\n\tconstiterator_find(map);\r\n\titerator_find(map);\r\n\treturn 0;\r\n}\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\r\nThe command to compile it is something like `g++ ahm_bench.cpp -o3 -lmimalloc -I ./godottest -I ./godot/platform/linuxbsd/ -o ahm_bench`\r\n\r\nMight be slightly inaccurate since I couldn't find a way to use Godot's own allocator from outside like this. Hence why I used a high perfomance allocator like `mimalloc`.\r\n\r\nOver 5 alternated runs, results in seconds:\r\n\r\n### Filled `get()`\r\n\r\n| `master` | PR |\r\n|-|-|\r\n|4.90\t|4.59\r\n|4.89\t|4.61\r\n|4.93\t|4.59\r\n|4.92\t|4.58\r\n|4.90\t|4.59\r\n\r\n\r\n### Filled `getptr()`\r\n| `master` | PR |\r\n|-|-|\r\n|4.91\t|4.60\r\n|4.93\t|4.59\r\n|4.95\t|4.61\r\n|4.92\t|4.59\r\n|4.91\t|4.60\r\n\r\n### Filled `has()`\r\n| `master` | PR |\r\n|-|-|\r\n|4.74\t|4.60\r\n|4.75\t|4.55\r\n|4.75\t|4.58\r\n|4.79\t|4.57\r\n|4.75\t|4.60\r\n\r\n### Filled `ConstIterator find()`\r\n| `master` | PR |\r\n|-|-|\r\n|5.84\t|5.28\r\n|5.89\t|5.27\r\n|5.85\t|5.27\r\n|5.87\t|5.27\r\n|5.85\t|5.30\r\n\r\n### Filled `Iterator find()`\r\n| `master` | PR |\r\n|-|-|\r\n|5.19\t|4.93\r\n|5.18\t|4.92\r\n|5.16\t|4.89\r\n|5.15\t|4.90\r\n|5.13\t|4.88\r\n\r\n### Empty `getptr()`\r\n| `master` | PR |\r\n|-|-|\r\n|0.192\t|0.185\r\n|0.192\t|0.185\r\n|0.205\t|0.193\r\n|0.195\t|0.184\r\n|0.193\t|0.183\r\n\r\n### Empty `has()`\r\n| `master` | PR |\r\n|-|-|\r\n|0.189\t|0.174\r\n|0.187\t|0.174\r\n|0.194\t|0.189\r\n|0.187\t|0.174\r\n|0.186\t|0.173\r\n\r\n### Empty `ConstIterator find()`\r\n| `master` | PR |\r\n|-|-|\r\n|0.489\t|0.483\r\n|0.491\t|0.471\r\n|0.506\t|0.485\r\n|0.498\t|0.469\r\n|0.482\t|0.477\r\n\r\n### Empty `Iterator find()`\r\n| `master` | PR |\r\n|-|-|\r\n|0.327\t|0.333\r\n|0.325\t|0.330\r\n|0.342\t|0.333\r\n|0.330\t|0.325\r\n|0.319\t|0.324\r\n\r\n### Caveats\r\n\r\nLinux builds with `target=template_release production=yes` had a 4KiB increase in size. ","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":3240950060,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMjQwOTUwMDYw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/performance","name":"performance","description":"","color":"447777","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2025-11-23T23:53:33Z","updated_at":"2026-09-02T07:27:00Z","closed_at":"2026-09-01T21:12:59Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_r